ZTEXT00100001346fede108c0000000
Zero UEFI loader audit - 2026-11-15

Scope: loader.zero only. LANGUAGE.ztext and UEFI-NOTES.ztext were reviewed before
editing. The loader remains entirely Zero and uses the compiler's documented
Microsoft x64 call primitive for firmware interfaces. No C, Python, assembly
loader, external bootloader, or runtime implementation was introduced.

Fixed defects

1. SetWatchdogTimer failure was overwritten by HandleProtocol. Its result now
   gates all subsequent setup and reports pre-exit stage 0 on non-success.
2. The old read-completion sentinel status=2 collided with EFI warning 2. A
   warning from an earlier protocol or allocation could reach File.Close with
   no valid file, and a read warning could continue with incomplete code.
   Completion now has a separate flag. Every service still requires exact
   EFI_SUCCESS (0); warnings are deliberately rejected, never reinterpreted as
   internal control flow. Only validated positive read lengths advance the
   received count. Empty/oversized files, early EOF and oversized read counts
   use EFI_LOAD_ERROR, not a positive warning value.
3. Stage 10 previously emitted ':' through '0'+10. Stage diagnostics now
   produce decimal 0..10, and every diagnostic byte waits for UART readiness.
4. Final memory-map and exit failures previously halted silently. The UART
   now identifies GetMemoryMap failure, an invalid map, ExitBootServices
   failure, or exhaustion of four invalid-key retries. Map size must fit the
   existing 64 KiB buffer, descriptor size must be at least 40, and at least
   one descriptor must fit in the returned size.

Final source review

The kernel path remains UTF-16 \\kernel.bin. Allocations remain 32 executable
LoaderCode pages, 64 LoaderData stack pages, and 17 LoaderData pages for the
handoff plus memory map. Handoff offsets and enter(code,handoff,stack+262144)
are unchanged. Kernel reads are bounded by the validated 131072-byte file
limit, reject zero progress, and cannot advance beyond that limit.

Files close before final map acquisition. Only the existing GetMemoryMap and
ExitBootServices calls occur in the final retry loop: no added protocol,
console, allocation, file, or other firmware service runs after the first
exit attempt. The map capacity is restored for each attempt, its returned key
is passed to ExitBootServices without intervening firmware calls, and only
EFI_INVALID_PARAMETER permits retry. Four unsuccessful exit attempts stop.
Successful exit enters the kernel immediately, disabling interrupts through
the documented enter primitive. Failure diagnostics use direct COM1 I/O and
retain a per-byte poll limit of 1000000 iterations before halting.

Build verification

Command: ./build/zero --efi < loader.zero > build/loader-audit.efi
Result: compiler exit 0; 9216-byte x86-64 PE32+ EFI application, two sections.
No BOOTX64.EFI, system.img, compiler, kernel, or image-builder source was
modified by this audit.

Source SHA-256:
3d83a0a3880fff15ad8c76882ad222db6b030f60ec2baa9074cb12c6f90048e8
Audit EFI SHA-256:
c417eeef244d0522de306b11ee5fe96ea2170fce1d22da1adf4d93c3cc8ee888

Runtime verification

PASS: nine QEMU 10.0.13/OVMF boots with 128 MiB, pc/TCG, COM1 output, and
snapshot-mode data disk. Eight temporary Zero source variants exercised
specific failure paths; the ninth used unmodified loader.zero and reached
the kernel terminal. Temporary FAT images were generated with our existing
Zero image builder. Every expected line appeared; no failure case reached
the kernel terminal. The test processes were stopped by a 20-second timeout
after observing their terminal/halt state.

Injected condition                     Observed loader diagnostic
Watchdog EFI_DEVICE_ERROR               failed before exit; stage=0
Initial HandleProtocol warning 2        failed before exit; stage=1
File.Read warning 2                     failed before exit; stage=7
Handoff allocation OUT_OF_RESOURCES     failed before exit; stage=10
GetMemoryMap BUFFER_TOO_SMALL           GetMemoryMap failed
Successful map, descriptor size zero   invalid memory map
ExitBootServices EFI_DEVICE_ERROR       ExitBootServices failed
Real ExitBootServices, wrong map key    ExitBootServices retry limit
Unmodified loader                      kernel serial terminal ready

The wrong-key case called real firmware with each acquired key plus one;
it therefore exercised reacquisition and UART output after failed real exit
attempts. Other faults were deterministic status/output substitutions in
temporary Zero source copies, not claims of hardware firmware failures.
Tests/scripts/logs reside in /tmp/zero-loader-audit in this execution
workspace; their source variants are not the production loader. Hardware,
firmware without COM1, and arbitrary malformed firmware pointers were not
tested. The fixed memory-map capacity and strict warning policy are retained
intentional limits; exceeding that capacity now gives a visible failure.
